WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Paris 2024, Olympic opening ceremony.

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.300
Aya Nakamura, born in Mali,

3
00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:09.600
sings with the band of
the «Garde républicaine».

4
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Then Céline Dion, from Quebec,

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.830
sings from the Eiffel Tower.

6
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.260
So who represents France?

7
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.750
On the radio, a law from
1994 sets its own rule.

8
00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.190
Why would a country tell
its radio stations to play

9
00:00:23.190 --> 00:00:25.460
a set share of songs in French,

10
00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.470
and does that still matter?

11
00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:30.370
In this mission, you'll
map French-speaking music,

12
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:34.060
then travel from «la
chanson à texte» to rap.

13
00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.160
Then you'll weigh both sides:

14
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.050
«les quotas aident les jeunes artistes»,

15
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:40.740
or have quotas lost their point?

16
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:43.730
Your mission: find out
why the rule exists,

17
00:00:43.730 --> 00:00:45.710
and decide whether it still matters.
